    "http://jobs.ecenglish.com": {
      "title": "Work with us",
      "description": "Work for EC - Careers at EC English Language Centres Skip to content 💬 Not sure which course is right? Our team can help. Destinations USA → Learn English in Boston Learn English in Boston, one of America’s most historic and student-friendly cities. Prices start at $505 → Learn English in Los Angeles Learn English in Los Angeles, one of America’s most vibrant, multicultural cities. Prices start at $420 → Learn English in New York Learn English in New York, a global cosmopolitan hub for culture, arts, entertainment and commerce. Prices start at $500 → Learn English in New York for Adults (30+) Learn English in New York for adults (30+) at a school only for mature students who want to study with ambitious, like-minded professionals. $500 → Learn English in San Diego Learn English in San Diego, one of America’s friendliest, most laid-back coastal cities and home to Southern California’s best beaches. Prices start at $370 → Learn English in San Francisco Learn English in San Francisco and immerse yourself in one of America’s most creative, innovative and open-minded cities. Prices start at $455 Learn English in the USA Canada → Learn English in Montreal Discover the joy of learning French in Montreal, the world’s largest bilingual city, renowned for its rich history and enchanting old-world charm → Prices start at C$420 → Learn English in Toronto Learn English in Toronto, Canada’s largest city and one of the most multicultural cities in the world Prices start at C$435 → Learn English in Toronto for Adults (30+) Learn English in Toronto for adults (30+) at a school exclusively for mature students who want to study with ambitious, likeminded professionals. Prices start at C$435 → Learn English in Vancouver Learn English in Vancouver, a friendly, relaxed seaport city on Canada’s west coast. Prices start at C$435 → Learn English in Vancouver for Adults (30+) Learn English in Vancouver for adults (30+) at a school exclusively for mature students who want to study with likeminded professionals. Prices start at C$435 → Learn French in Montreal Discover the joy of learning French in Montreal, the world’s largest bilingual city, renowned for its rich history and enchanting old-world charm. Prices start at C$420 Learn English in Canada United Kingdom → Learn English in Brighton Known as ‘London by the Sea’, Brighton offers the cultural vibe of nearby London in a laid-back seaside environment. Prices start at £385 → Learn English in Brighton for Adults (30+) Learn English in Brighton for adults (30+) at a school created exclusively for mature adults who want to study with likeminded professionals. Prices start at £405 → Learn English in Cambridge Learn English in Cambridge, a picturesque, historic university town and the UK’s most prestigious academic hotspot. Prices start at £375 → Learn English in London Learn English in London, one of the most extraordinary cities in the world. Prices start at £405 → Learn English in London for Adults (30+) Learn English in London for adults (30+) at a school exclusively for mature students who want to study with ambitious, likeminded professionals. Prices start at £405 → Learn English in Manchester Learn English in Manchester, a top student city in the UK that’s known for its enterprising creativity. Prices start at £380 Learn English in the United Kingdom Ireland → Learn English in Dublin Learn English in Dublin, Ireland’s lively capital, and discover a city renowned for its relaxed vibe, charming character and hospitable locals. Prices start at €380 → Learn English in Dublin for Adults (30+) Learn English in Dublin for adults (30+) at a school created exclusively for mature adults who want to study with likeminded professionals. Prices start at €380 Learn English in Ireland Malta → Learn English in Malta Learn English in Malta, a charming island country in the Mediterranean known for its rich history and stunning beaches. Prices start at €300 → Learn English in Malta for Adults (30+) Learn English in Malta for adults (30+) at a school exclusively for mature students who want to study with likeminded professionals. Prices start at €300 Learn English on the Maltese Islands South Africa → Learn English in Cape Town Learn English in Cape Town and immerse yourself in the natural wonders of South Africa. Prices start at €345 → Learn English in Cape Town for Adults (30+) Learn English in Cape Town for adults (30+) at a school exclusively for mature students who want to study with likeminded professionals. Prices start at €345 Learn English in South Africa United Arab Emirates → Learn English in Dubai Learn English in Dubai, a global center of commerce, luxury and tourism, and immerse yourself in a modern metropolis with a timeless sensibility. Prices start at $380 Learn English in  United Arab Emirates View all Destinations Our Support Your success is our priority. From visas guidance to accommodation, we’ve got you covered! Learn more Courses General English Courses → General English Cover the bases of speaking, listening, reading, and writing. Prices start at €300 → English in the City Learn English on the go and see a new city up-close. Prices start at €420 → Bilingual Programme in Montreal English and French courses in the world’s largest bilingual city. Prices start at C$435 → Bildungsurlaub Programme English programmes for German workers on educational leave. Prices start at €300 → Mini Group Benefit from accelerated results in our small group English classes. Prices start at €495 → Writing with AI Write better English using AI tools like ChatGPT. Prices start at €410 English for Business Courses → English for Work Build confidence in your professional comunication and correspondence skills. Prices start at €410 → Business English for 25+ For professionals with Upper Intermediate to Advanced English proficiency. Prices start at €410 → Business English Mini Group Master Business English in our concentrated, tailored Mini Groups. Prices start at €540 → English for Business Courses Education & Exam Preparation → Academic Semester or Year Learn English over a semester/year, unlock life-long opportunities. Prices start at €5,760 → Cambridge Exam Preparation Expert guidance and personalised support for your Cambridge Exam. Prices start at €410 → IELTS Exam Preparation One of the world’s most trusted language qualifications. Prices start at €1,640 → TOEFL Exam Preparation Get into your dream university with the TOEFL. Prices start at $1,000 → TOEIC Exam Preparation Prove your proficiency in an international workplace with the TOEIC. Prices start at C$1,740 → English Now Customise your curriculum with focused module options at EC Cambridge. Prices start at £710 → University Pathways Programmes designed to help you access an overseas university education. Education & Exams Preparation Courses English Plus → English & Dance in New York Supplementary dance classes, including ballet, hip-hop, and more. Prices start at $500 → English & Safari Combine English with a safari experience at EC Cape Town. Prices start at €345 → English & Surfing Enjoy regular surf lessons on San Diego’s famous beaches. Prices start at $370 → Flexi Track Benefit from personalised attention and flexible scheduling at EC Cambridge. Prices start at £515 → One-to-One Add One-to-one sessions to any EC course. Prices start at €190 → Writing with AI Improve your written English with artificial intelligence tools like ChatGPT. Prices start at €410 View all Adult Courses Erasmus → Erasmus Plus for Teachers Hone your skills as an education professional in Malta or Dublin. → Erasmus Plus for teachers English and Digital Skills Obtain the digital skills necessary to lead today’s classroom. → Erasmus Plus for teachers English and Teaching Methodology General English lessons blended with novel teaching methodology skills. EC Escapes (50+) → EC Escapes: Malta Immersive language vacation on this sun-splashed Mediterranean island. Prices start at €695 → EC Escapes: London Immersive language vacation in the cosmopolitan cultural hub of London. Prices start at £730 → EC Escapes: Brighton Immersive language vacation in Brighton on England’s south coast. → EC Escapes: Dublin Immersive language vacation in the lively, friendly, culturally-enriching city. Prices start at €755 → EC Escapes: Cape Town Immersive language vacation in this beautiful ‘Mother City’. Prices start at €695 → EC Escapes: New York Immersive language vacation in the US’s cultural and economic centre. Prices start at $905 EC Escapes: Language Vacations French Courses → General French Improve your overall French language skills in Montreal. Prices start at C$420 → French Academic Semester or Year Your long-term path to French fluency in Montreal. Prices start at C$8,640 View all French Courses Learn English Online (EC Live) CELTA & DELTA Toronto CELTA Our part-time CELTA courses in Toronto are officially approved by Cambridge Assessment English. London CELTA The twelve-week course is suitable for people who are interested in learning to teach. Toronto DELTA Delta at EC combines seminars and lectures with teaching practice. London DELTA Gaining a Diploma in English Language Teaching to Adults (DELTA) qualification requires significant time and effort. Teacher Training View all Courses Our Support Your success is our priority. From visas guidance to accommodation, we’ve got you covered! Learn more Online Courses Blog Schools USA → Boston → Los Angeles → New York → New York (30+) → San Diego → San Francisco Learn English in the USA Canada → Montreal → Toronto → Toronto for Adults (30+) → Vancouver → Vancouver for Adults (30+) Learn English in the Canada UK → Brighton → Brighton (30+) → Cambridge → London → London (30+) → Manchester Learn English in the United Kingdom Ireland → Dublin → Dublin (30+) Learn English in Ireland Malta → Malta → Malta (30+) Learn English on the Maltese Islands South Africa → Cape Town → Cape Town (30+) Learn English in South Africa UAE → Dubai Learn English in the United Arab Emirates View all Destinations Our Support Your success is our priority. From visas guidance to accommodation, we’ve got you covered! Learn more Courses General English Courses General English English in the City Bilingual Programme in Montreal Bildungsurlaub Programme Mini Group Flexi Track Writing with AI Business English English for Work Business English for 25+ Business English Mini Group English for Business Courses Exam Preparation Academic Semester or Year Cambridge Exam Preparation IELTS Exam Preparation TOEFL Exam Preparation TOEIC Exam Preparation English Now Education & Exams Preparation Courses English Plus English & Dance in New York English & Safari One-to-One Writing with AI View all Adult Courses Erasmus Erasmus Plus for Teachers Erasmus Plus for teachers English and Digital Skills Erasmus Plus for teachers English and Teaching Methodology Our Support Your success is our priority. From visas guidance to accommodation, we’ve got you covered! Learn more EC Escapes → Malta (50+) → London (50+) → Brighton (50+) → Dublin (50+) → Cape Town (50+) → New York (50+) EC Escapes: Language Vacations Our Support Your success is our priority. From visas guidance to accommodation, we’ve got you covered! Learn more EC Live Brochures Visas Sign in My EC Staff Default Mode Agent Mode Contact Us GET A QUOTE Partners Area Agent Portal Language English العربية English Français Deutsch Italiano 日本語 Português Русский Español Contact Search Contact Us GET A QUOTE Partners Area Agent Portal Sign in My EC Staff Agent Mode Default Mode English العربية English Français Deutsch Italiano 日本語 Português Русский Español Menu Cancel Home About us Work with us Work with us Help us to help students across the globe Excellent Our values underpin everything we do We love teaching, we deliver on our promises and we do whatever it takes to ensure our students achieve success. If you want to work to the same high standards, then take a look at our latest vacancies. Be a leader Leadership isn’t restricted to the top; we are leaders at every level. We motivate those around us, we take action, we seek opportunity. We all have the authority to lead by example. Be an innovator We’re passionate about improving ourselves and inspire others to do the same. We take delight in discovery; personal, educational and technological. We are creative, and problem solve every day. We are curious and empathetic. We are innovators. Be genuine It is as important to hold our hands up to mistakes as it is to celebrate our successes. We keep it transparent, we keep it honest, we keep it real. We are authentic. Be knowledgeable We know a great deal about language education and are proud to share it. We empower others with our knowledge. If we don’t know, we ask. We never stop learning, never stop thinking and never stop sharing. Be inspirational Inspiration runs deep in us all. After all, we make dreams come true every day. We open doors. We build bridges and break down walls. We provide life-changing experiences. We are inspiring people. Be a storyteller We all have an EC story to tell. We all have our histories, our first days, our funniest moments. Storytelling is the oldest form of education. Share your stories, share your ideas, share your knowledge. Tell your story. Wellbeing at EC At EC, we are dedicated to cultivating a culture of holistic wellbeing where every member of our diverse community feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. We recognise that prioritising mental health and wellbeing not only fosters individual resilience but also enhances productivity, creativity, and overall job satisfaction. Apart from working in an inclusive and open environment, we offer a comprehensive Employee Assistance Programme, providing confidential and professional counselling services to support our team members and their families. Our robust wellbeing policy ensures that our employees’ mental and physical health remains our top priority. Additionally, we organise regular wellbeing activities and training sessions to foster a healthy and supportive work environment. Join us and be a part of a company that truly values and invests in the wellbeing of its employees. Applicant Help We understand that sometimes questions arise whilst applying for a position. We’re here to help. Contact us if you have any questions. hrhelpdesk@ecenglish.com Current Vacancies Check our open positions Powered by Looking for summer work? A range of positions are available in management, academics or leisure, with vacancies in the UK, USA, Canada & Malta through our Young Learners programme – Embassy Summer . View jobs and apply Accredited by About EC Home Accreditations About us Agents & Partners Industry Awards The EC Promise MyEC Work with us Under 18s at EC Schools Code of Conduct Contact us Courses Bildungsurlaub Programme English Courses English for Work English for Business Courses Education & Exams Preparation Courses Erasmus+ English Courses Online English Courses General English Teaching Methods Teacher Training Virtual Internships Special Focus Classes Learners Support Learn English for Free Visa Information Frequently Asked Questions Orange Carpet Experience Student Insurance Staff Login Policy Documents Accommodation USA Canada UK Ireland Malta South Africa United Arab Emirates Young Learners 7+ Adults 16+ Adults 30+ Adults 50+ Teacher training © EC English Language Centres Terms and Conditions Privacy Policy Cookie Policy EC English Holdings Ltd: EC Central ‘Language House’, Marguerite Mangion Street, St. Julians, STJ 3180, Malta"
    },
    "https://www.fredonia.edu/student-life/career-development-office/student-employment": {
      "title": "Student Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Student Employment Opportunities | Fredonia.edu Skip to main content News/Events Map/Tour Give Info For Current Students Incoming Students Parents/Families Faculty/Staff Alumni Bicentennial Celebration Apply Click to go to the homepage. News/Events Map/Tour Give Info For Current Students Incoming Students Parents/Families Faculty/Staff Alumni Bicentennial Celebration Apply About Fast Facts Events Calendar Community Diversity and Inclusion Leadership Academics Majors & Programs Summer Sessions Winter Session J-Term Study Abroad Academic Advising Continuing & Community Ed Admissions Accepted Students First-Year Transfer International Graduate Visit Fredonia Virtual Tour Scholarships & Aid Financial Aid Scholarships Student Life Housing Dining Clubs & Organizations Health, Wellness & Support Athletics & Recreation × search Student Employment Opportunities More In This Section Click to expose navigation links on mobile. Home About CDO Services and Staff CDO Mission For Students & Alumni Schedule an Appointment FREDNetwork Careers & Majors Internships Job Search Resumes & Cover Letter Interviews Credentials File Get Connected Graduate School Request a CDO Presentation For Employers Host an Intern Post a Job CDO Spotlight Program Employer-in-Residence Program Recruit on Campus Consortium Services Academic Programs Report a Hire Campus Maps About the Area For Parents Career Planning Checklist For Parents of Prospective College Students Career Planning Course for Parents For Faculty & Staff Internship Forms Developing New Internships Request a CDO Presentation Contact Looking for an on campus or local student job opportunity? Login with Fredonia e-services ID and Password Select JOBS in the left navigation, then enter FREDONIA in the search bar or location search to explore on-campus and local opportunities. If a position is not posted in Handshake, please contact the office or employer directly to inquire. NOTE: The needs of each office/agency can change quickly, and their job postings may not always be updated regularly. Review a contact list of on-campus and local employers accessible along the Campus & Community Bus Schedule route . In-person or direct contact is recommended to develop a quick connection and demonstrate interest & initiative! Next Steps To discuss your options, develop some strategies, and learn how the CDO can help, schedule an appointment to meet with a career counselor. Federal work study positions are available and are coordinated through the Financial Aid Office. Early FAFSA application is critical every year. For more information, please visit the Federal Work-Study page. Student Payroll Information SUNY Policy on Student Assistant Employees You may also be interested in the following resources: Vacancy Links Summer Job Links Employer Directories & Websites Transportation Resources Campus Carpooling Program - FREDRide SUNY Fredonia - 511 NY Ride Share Chautauqua Area Regional Transit (CARTS) - Schedules, Requests & more! Career Development Office Gregory Hall, 2nd floor State University of New York at Fredonia Fredonia, NY 14063 Contact 716-673-3327 716-673-3593 f careers@fredonia.edu Hours Academic-Year Hours: 8:00 am - 4:30 pm, Monday-Friday Summer Hours: 8:00 am - 4:00 pm, Monday-Friday Contact Us | 716-673-3111 Campus Map Who do I contact for ... ? Emergencies & Closings Faculty/Staff Directory Careers Logins Email FREDLearn fredPASS My.FRED Starfish YourConnection Tracker Answers Drupal Login Drupal Help Click to go to the homepage. © 2025 State University of New York at Fredonia - 280 Central Avenue - Fredonia, NY Non-Discrimination Statement | Campus Safety Report | Privacy | Accessibility We use cookies on this site to enhance your user experience By clicking any link on this page you are giving your consent for us to set cookies. OK, I Agree"
    },
    "https://www.rfsuny.org/about-us/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers - RF for SUNY Menu Search RF Website RF Connect Policies, Procedures, Forms Speak Up RF - Ethics Hotline 800.461.9330 SUNY Inventor Portal A-Z SUNY.EDU About Us Who We Are Leadership Founding Documents Mission, Vision and Values Careers Fast Facts Contact Us Reports & Publications RF Brochure Corporate Fact Sheet SUNY Research in the News Our Work What We Do Operating Plan Sponsored Programs Administration Innovation and Partnerships Research Learning & Development Compliance Legal Counsel Internal Audit Tools & Applications RF Connect RF Report Center Pre-Award and Compliance System (PACS) Oracle Business Applications Self Service Certify Your Effort (ECC) SUNY Inventor Portal Oracle Process Help Oracle Report Help Oracle List of Value Definitions Information For Principal Investigators Operations Managers Research Administrators HR Administrators Students Sponsors Vendors Employees Retirees SUNY RF About Us Careers Our people are our top priority . They are our greatest strength, our most valuable asset. It’s our responsibility to invest the time and create an environment for our talent and business to succeed together . Our commitment to employee growth, forging a sustainable career path, and striving for operational excellence in all that we do. Some people call it a community . Some call it a second family . Intern With Us! Veterans Work & Life Balance The RF ranks among the top five in most benefits based on a recent survey of its peer groups including active employee and post-retirement health insurance. Meaningful Work As an RF employee, you are part of a team whose vision is to make SUNY the best place for faculty, students and staff to solve the world's most pressing problems. Professional Development Job Skills and Supervisory Training, Leadership Master Classes, Mentoring Programs, Professional Development Scholarships, 100+ archived video-based learning programs and more! Employee Support Free long-term disability benefits for qualified full-time employees. The RF offers employer paid life insurance with additional optional low-cost group term life insurance. Education Planning The RF is an eligible employer under the Public Student Loan Forgiveness program and offers college savings plans and a tuition waiver program. Family Support Up to $800 toward funding of dependent care expenses,  allowing employees to set aside pre-tax dollars for qualified out-of-pocket childcare and medical expenses. As an Equal Opportunity / Affirmative Action Employer , The Research Foundation for SUNY will not discriminate in its employment practices due to an applicant's race, color, creed, religion, sex, pregnancy-related conditions, reproductive health decisions, childbirth or related medical conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, transgender status, age, national origin or ancestry, marital status, familial status, citizenship, physical and mental disability, prior arrest or conviction record, genetic characteristics/genetic information, predisposition or carrier status, domestic violence victim status, military status or service, veteran status, or any other characteristics protected under federal, state or local law. Quick Links SUNYRF Corporate Office Job Openings SUNYRF Campus Job Openings Benefits Diversity and Inclusion Affirmative Action Resources Equal Employment Opportunity: Know Your Rights Poster Equal Employment Opportunity and Antidiscrimination Policy Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement EEO Self-Identification Form - Applicants Pay Transparency Nondiscrimination Statement RF Employment Application 10 Perks of Working at the RF Employee Links Employee Center Vacation, Sick and Personal Paid Time Off Contacts Click for More Facebook Twitter Linkedin YouTube Information For Principal Investigators RF Report Center Verify Your Effort (eCRT) Self Service SUNY Inventor Portal Policies A to Z Procedures A to Z Policies & Procedures by Topic or Business Area SUNY Statement on Research Integrity More... Operations Managers Policies A to Z Procedures A to Z Policies & Procedures by Topic or Business Area Verify Your Effort (ECC) Self Service SUNY Inventor Portal More... Research Administrators RF Report Center Verify Your Effort (ECC) Self Service SUNY Inventor Portal Policies A to Z Procedures A to Z Policies & Procedures by Topic or Business Area More... Business and Industry Available Technologies Technology Accelerator Fund (TAF) SUNY Insure Diversity and Inclusion Affirmative Action Students SUNY Diversity and Inclusion Affirmative Action SUNY Research Sponsors Policies A to Z Procedures A to Z Policies & Procedures by Topic or Business Area Corporate Fact Sheet RF Operating Plan Sponsored Programs Activity Report A-133 Annual Report & Certification IRS Non-Profit Tax-Exempt (Form 990) Diversity and Inclusion Affirmative Action Contacts Vendors Corporate Fact Sheet Doing Business With the RF Open Requests for Goods and Services (RFPs) Purchase Order Terms Electronic Payment Information Tax Related Information Diversity and Inclusion Affirmative Action Contacts Employees Self Service Your RF Benefits Taxation & Reporting Learning & Development More... Retirees Retiree Benefits Handbook More... Research Locations Directory Medium Example Choose a location This is another option too Look, a third option Currently Displaying SUNY System Administration State University Plaza 353 Broadway Albany, NY 12246 (518) 320-1100 RF A-Z Applications Available Technologies Benefits Code of Conduct Corporate Fact Sheet Careers Diversity and Inclusion Doing Business With RF Financials 101 Innovation and Partnerships Learning & Development Leadership Policies & Procedures Sponsored Programs Administration Strategic Plan Self Service MORE... Working at the RF Contact Us Main Number (518) 434-7000 Directions & Parking RF Style & Standards Website Feedback Privacy Policy / Terms of Use Copyright © 2026 SUNY RF. All Rights Reserved."
